{:edb/db-before-t 1989 :edb/db-after-t 1990 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535302 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:39:40.791Z" 13194139535302 true] [17592186083166 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342763 13194139535302 true] [17592186083167 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342770 13194139535302 true] [17592186083168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342777 13194139535302 true] [17592186083168 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342784 13194139535302 true] [17592186083564 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535302 true] [17592186083564 1100 "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-t,\\,2{t}^{2}-4t+2⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=2.$" 13194139535302 true] [17592186083564 1100 "A particle $P$ is moving in the $x$-$y$ plane. Its position vector relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by\n\n$r = ⟨t^{3} - 2t^{2} - t, 2t^{2} - 4t + 2⟩, t > 0$.\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t = 2$." 13194139535302 false] [17592186083564 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}-4t+2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t-1,4t-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨3(2)^{2}-4(2)-1,4(2)-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=2$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(2),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(2)| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342763 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342764 13194139535302 true] [17592186342763 1089 "q-121717" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342763 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535302 true] [17592186342763 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\sqrt{4t+1},3t-2⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the velocity vector $v$ at time $t=2.$" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342763 1113 #uuid "04e13fd6-9b6c-5320-b070-cd6f7b64eb13" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342763 1145 "The particle's velocity vector is given by the derivative of its position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{4t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4t+1}},3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=2,$ we substitute into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4(2)+1}},3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}},3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342765 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342766 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342767 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342768 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342769 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1041 "selection" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342766 13194139535302 true] [17592186342764 1110 #uuid "cbe41e6f-133b-517c-85be-d9e88e35dd11" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342765 1034 "v(2)=⟨3,2⟩" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342765 1111 #uuid "62d988ce-7055-5dab-854b-dbfcf9561136" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342766 1034 "v(2)=⟨\\frac{2}{3},3⟩" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342766 1111 #uuid "2b56afd4-dfbf-54fa-8b47-1951aaa8eee1" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342767 1034 "v(2)=⟨\\frac{4}{3},3⟩" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342767 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342767 1111 #uuid "42fa4738-f43d-5c85-b563-2e9ccede4609" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342768 1034 "v(2)=⟨1,3⟩" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342768 1111 #uuid "054f8b35-37f5-5d0b-a90a-573aaa235537" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342769 1034 "v(2)=⟨\\frac{2}{3},2⟩" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342769 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342769 1111 #uuid "32f50140-03af-5080-9774-aae2cd6586da" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342770 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342771 13194139535302 true] [17592186342770 1089 "q-121730" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342770 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535302 true] [17592186342770 1100 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342770 1113 #uuid "b9e2e9d7-7206-54bd-8133-c43a9871dfd4" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342770 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\pi ,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\pi ) & =⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩=⟨-4,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=\\pi $ we calculate the magnitude of $v(\\pi ),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(\\pi )| & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed when $t=\\pi $ is $4.$" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342772 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342773 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342774 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342775 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342776 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1041 "selection" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342775 13194139535302 true] [17592186342771 1110 #uuid "d0962e7f-c716-569b-ac93-c27db645b4a0" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342772 1034 "\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342772 1111 #uuid "12435079-d19e-5ffc-8ae6-38b74b4da42f" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342773 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342773 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342773 1111 #uuid "16db51d7-5f3b-5f12-8b31-e7283fea8ee3" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342774 1034 "2" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342774 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342774 1111 #uuid "54caf6ed-b72d-55b8-9639-eb529ca5484b" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342775 1034 "4" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342775 1111 #uuid "566dc172-c0fd-5437-8058-aaa44298ad94" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342776 1034 "5" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342776 1111 #uuid "e53547ec-5b80-57a7-891b-5a8b778e6b01" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342777 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342778 13194139535302 true] [17592186342777 1089 "q-121739" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342777 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535302 true] [17592186342777 1100 "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{2}-6t,(t-3)^{5}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139535302 true] [17592186342777 1113 #uuid "e25e0179-be85-5825-a6d6-eefada53b4e2" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342777 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-6t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-3)^{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-6,5(t-3)^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2(t-3),5(t-3)^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2(t-3),5(t-3)^{4}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-3)=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=3, \\\\ 5(t-3)^{4}=0\\, & ⇒\\,t=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=3$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342779 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342780 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342781 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342782 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342783 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1041 "selection" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342783 13194139535302 true] [17592186342778 1110 #uuid "bf77831e-6e85-50c8-8e8a-fe8956f617d8" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342779 1034 "t=1" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342779 1111 #uuid "605cd42b-68ff-5a62-baae-385cc923602a" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342780 1034 "t=2" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342780 1111 #uuid "654fb3e3-066c-545e-bfb3-78caee10856f" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342781 1034 "t=4" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342781 1111 #uuid "b9caacc1-b6dc-5bf1-9d97-3ee15fe5da83" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342782 1034 "The particle is never stationary" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535302 true] [17592186342782 1111 #uuid "fecc0fef-48e4-55e6-b47f-f2b91fd85fd1" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342783 1034 "t=3" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342783 1111 #uuid "75dda238-1f7d-5cf4-bd3c-e6e7fd3f6d6f" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342784 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342785 13194139535302 true] [17592186342784 1089 "q-352611" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342784 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535302 true] [17592186342784 1100 "A particle $P$ moves in the $x$-$y$ plane (relative to a fixed origin $O$) with position vector\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+1},\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+5}⟩,\\,t\\in [0,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate the times at which the particle is stationary.\n\nThe particle is stationary at $t=$  \n{{field-1}}." 13194139535302 true] [17592186342784 1113 #uuid "182941c7-4ee6-503e-a745-3ad3bae7e902" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342784 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3(t-2)^{2}}{t+5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3(t-2)(t+4)}{(t+1)^{2}},\\frac{3(t-2)(t+12)}{(t+5)^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe particle is stationary when its velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\frac{3(t-2)(t+4)}{(t+1)^{2}},\\frac{3(t-2)(t+12)}{(t+5)^{2}}⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(t-2)(t+4)}{(t+1)^{2}}=0\\, & ⇒\\,3(t-2)(t+4)=0\\,⇒\\,t=2,-4, \\\\ \\frac{3(t-2)(t+12)}{(t+5)^{2}}=0\\, & ⇒\\,3(t-2)(t+12)=0\\,⇒\\,t=2,-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $t=2$ is the only solution that satisfies both equations, so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139535302 true] [17592186342785 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342786 13194139535302 true] [17592186342785 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535302 true] [17592186342785 1041 "field-1" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342785 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342786 13194139535302 true] [17592186342785 1110 #uuid "402cfa08-b520-55b1-9ae2-b86eff3f1e46" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342786 1034 "2" 13194139535302 true] [17592186342786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535302 true] [17592186342786 1111 #uuid "7c776a09-e4d0-5965-af20-3e036e3b0fb9" 13194139535302 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-121717" 17592186342763 "q-121717/selection" 17592186342764 "q-121717/selection/601119bf001d9e7012b3e973af54b7d66a621e7fa3fcef39ceea29cfbf0833bc" 17592186342765 "q-121717/selection/65602e82cac46da550cb6d473d0f2593d0dce8b782c7476afd93097a079734b0" 17592186342766 "q-121717/selection/8979388da21670cd3070a6776f212b5c45d798469b729282bd5f47545984973a" 17592186342767 "q-121717/selection/a0fc969892e507d6f32e31ace3cd7513e02101ee5a2c61039d3a27744832315c" 17592186342768 "q-121717/selection/bc83fd7721319223a974b8d45ca5ce240ae34fd1c244fb225212f136119a802a" 17592186342769 "q-121730" 17592186342770 "q-121730/selection" 17592186342771 "q-121730/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" 17592186342772 "q-121730/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" 17592186342773 "q-121730/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" 17592186342774 "q-121730/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" 17592186342775 "q-121730/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" 17592186342776 "q-121739" 17592186342777 "q-121739/selection" 17592186342778 "q-121739/selection/24b44